A||||14||jd2m4||Why do people rain on my parade?||||1||
Z||000000||jd2m4||12-11-2001||10:50 PM||||I just joined this forum a few weeks ago,It's a great forum!I'm in the process of buying my old 85 2m4 back from a friend of mine that i sold it to.I think the clucth is bad,And the tranny needs rebuilding,But I'm not in a hurry to get the car running,So it will be a lenghty project.My garage has been converted to a office for my wife's paralegal business,so i have no place to work on the car,so i was going to leave the car at my mechanics house.Don't get me wrong he does excellent work (He did the build-up on my H.O. 305 in my firebird),But i can just hear him now-"why are you wasteing your time on a fiero" or "Why don't you go out and buy a real car"(his idea of a real car is a late 60's,early 70's car).I've always liked fiero's and i already have one v-8 car,So i wanted to do something with the fiero.You guys would laugh at some of the comments i have gotten,Some of you could probably even relate-one time i took my fiero the the muffler shop to get a performance muffler,This is the same shop i take my firebird to,and when i told the guy that "this is my fiero",he said You don't have much do you,I really had to resist the urge to punch him in his ignorant face!They act totally cool when i roll up in the firebird,But i show up in the fiero and all of a sudden i'm a 4th class citizen!I know i have some challenges ahead in the 85,the guy i sold it to had it painted florescent green(i have no problem with that color,But i like it better silver),and i'm probably looking at a tranny rebuild,but joining this board has really motivated me to do something with this car.I'll just have to ignore all the stupid remarks.Thanks everybody for listining  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever3000||12-11-2001||11:05 PM||||Now you know why we do as much of the work ourselves as possible (what? you think I <B>like</B> busted knuckles?).  I've been very fortunate to have received only positive remarks and respect from the two shops I frequent.  That's why I remain their customer.  If I heard some of the stuff you guys get at repair shops and parts stores, I don't know if I could control myself.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CheeverXmasSig.jpg">   <BR><I>Merry Christmas from the </I><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank><I>CFOG-I</I></A> <I>vice-president.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||12-12-2001||12:47 AM||||Just remember that ignorance is bliss and most of these idiots are pretty dog-gone blissfull ! ||||reg||4
Z||000003||artherd||12-12-2001||04:15 AM||||Every shop/parts store I visit the employees all want to know what kind of car that is, can't belive it's a Fiero when I tell them, and then their jaws hit the floor when I tell them about the silver Northstar car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I swear I've promised to bring the silver car by twenty shops when it's done, heh!<P>There was once a place I visited to get my car smogged.  Owner insulted my vehicle, so I called the CA BAR and reported the various volations I saw while I was there...  They were shut down within the week.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||12-12-2001||07:05 AM||||Yeah, they <B>are</B> a much-maligned little car, but I always take heart in the fact that since the general public just buys into the ignorance and automatically believes the garbage they hear, their ignorance keeps these cars (and their parts) at prices that are far more affordable for all of us who <B>do</B> appreciate them, and that's nothing but a good thing for all of us...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Can you imagine how expensive stuff would be if the Fiero was as sought-after as some of the more exotic cars? Or if we were in the same boat as the DeLorean owners? (Granted, there were only 8657 (give or take a few) DMC-12's made as opposed to 370,000+ Fieros made, but still, my wallet is deliriously happy that I don't own a DeLorean...)<P>The best way to fight the crap that is said to your face is to immediately take your business elsewhere. I mean right that moment - for example, if, when you go to the parts counter and the guy asks you what kind of car you have; you say "Fiero", he says, "I'm sorry..." - respond "I'd like to see the manager" or find him yourself if he's nearby, tell him exactly what just transpired, tell him you're a member of a Fiero club (well, Pennock's is *sort of* a club, right? &lt;g&gt; ) and that you are taking your business elsewhere since his employees are sarcastic and rude, and walk out the door. The potential for lost future sales to an unknown (possibly large?) quantity of (assumedly local) people, combined with the *actual* loss of a current sale will (if the shop is worth returning to anyway) warrant at the *very* least an 'attitude adjustment' for the smart-mouth employee.<P>Welcome to the fold...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show 2001||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-12-2001||07:31 AM||||Just be happy with what you like and %#@& everybody else. Remember some people like to spend thousands on Hyndais, Toyotas, and Hondas too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||12-12-2001||08:32 AM||||People gave me the same vibes too.  Why? why a Fiero?, why in the world are you going to paint it orange?  Now they all think it's pretty neat.<P>Good Luck with your Project!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerwinter3.gif">           <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.envy.nu/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A>||||reg||7
Z||000007||jd2m4||12-12-2001||09:23 AM||||Thanks for the inspiration!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000008||Bill Osmer||12-12-2001||01:25 PM||||Keep in mind that many people will respond to the CONDITION of a car - if it looks like a piece of ____, they'll treat it (and you) the same. If you bring it in looking clean and well-maintained (with no garbage falling out of the passenger seat!!), they'll look at the Fiero as a bright spot in their day. Never had a problem with any of the (few) shops I take mine to, but I also like working on it myself.<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000009||FieroMontreal||12-12-2001||02:49 PM||||Welcome!<P>So far I have brought my car to only 1 garage. Spent over $2500 getting it fixed in that garage over a 6 month time span.. My car was often referred to as "that POS at the end of the lot" ... but.. heh.. I knew he was kidding.. The guy had an 86 GT.. Came to some of our club meeting. Friendly people.. Well.. he doesn't work there anymore and the garage moved... and my car still isn't road worth..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Keep on Fieroing!<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontrealholidays.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000010||84Bill||12-12-2001||02:58 PM||||Welp you have 2 thing going for you.<BR>1 You found the best Fiero site on the net.<BR>2 Everyone here has an umbrella.<BR>So Welcome to the Forum and come on in from the rain and sit a spell.||||reg||14
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||12-12-2001||06:43 PM||||You forgot the third thing, 84Bill...<P>3. Everybody here is real good about sharing their umbrellas when needed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||8Ball||12-12-2001||07:13 PM||||My Fiero looks like crap atm and runs... well it runs and is my daily driver but deffinatly needs work. But I usually get pretty good remarks towards it like, WOW is that a Fiero?? or Oh man I haven't seen one of those in years, I always wanted one. When I am driving down the road ppl will slow down to get a look at my little car.<BR>It is a great feeling! But I have had a few ppl give me grief about it. And I ALWAYS set them straight. I can be a very outspoken person when I am insulted or confronted with ignorance.<BR>E.B.||||reg||1
Z||000013||2ndchancefiero||12-13-2001||01:06 AM|||| I have heard all the negative comments too, why a Fiero?..It will catch on fire..It's a death trap..etc..I have a 1971 Duster 340 and an 87GT Fiero and to tell the truth i'm having more fun driving the Fiero, and it's got power everything, handles better, stops better and it looks cool. In the end remember who cares what other people think or say as long as you like it.<P>------------------<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||8
